    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12-a2">

                <pb facs="0103" n="7" xml:id="pg7"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 416.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Spaulding to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Treasury Department</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1898-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November
                                17, 1898</hi></date>. (Received 10.35 a.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>This Department of opinion that clearance of Hawaiian schooner <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Americana</hi>, mentioned in your telegram of yesterday
                    afternoon, from St. John by Hawaiian consul should be recognized by Government
                    of Buenos Ayres and by United States minister and consul there, and that our
                    officers there should be instructed to act for Hawaii in such matters so far as
                    necessary and proper.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O. L. Spaulding</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
